Modified upstream components
============================

User-Scanner (https://github.com/kaifcodec/user-scanner), version 1.5.1.3,
is installed from its published wheel and carries its own MIT license, which
is reproduced below. The User-Scanner Docker image modifies the installed
package at build time (see "User-Scanner Docker/Dockerfile"):

  1. user_scanner/core/loud_prompt.py is overwritten with
     "User-Scanner Docker/hardening/loud_prompt.py". The replacement keeps the
     upstream function names and signatures (update_loud_module_preference,
     check_loud_module_permission) and part of the upstream skip message, so it
     is a MODIFIED version of the upstream file, not an independent work. It
     removes the interactive prompt and the saved-preference path; a loud
     module runs only when --allow-loud is passed.

  2. user_scanner/utils/update.py is overwritten with
     "User-Scanner Docker/hardening/update.py". The replacement keeps the
     upstream get_version helper shape and the update_self entry point, so it
     is a MODIFIED version of the upstream file, not an independent work.
     update_self now refuses to run (self-update is disabled in the image).

  3. user_scanner/user_scan/music/myspace.py is patched with sed to remove the
     ", verify=False" argument so TLS certificate verification stays on.

  4. The user-scanner-mcp console script is deleted from the image.

All other User-Scanner files are installed unmodified. The modified files in
this repository are distributed under the upstream MIT license for the
upstream-derived portions and under the Apache License 2.0 for the Hive
Controls additions.

